# Oldroyd-B 3D planar-extension analytical canary for the KRK-VE-3D dispatch.
# The production driver (run_viscoelastic_fvfd_extensional_3d) imposes the
# planar-extension velocity field u = (epsilon_dot*x, -epsilon_dot*y, 0) on a
# coarse box and advances psi = log(C) to the analytical fixed point. No
# obstacle or inflow/outflow geometry is needed: velocity_mode=:imposed.
#
# With lambda = 50 and epsilon_dot = 0.005, lambda*epsilon_dot = 0.25, so the
# Oldroyd-B planar-extension fixed point is
#   C_xx = 1/(1 - 2*lambda*epsilon_dot) = 2.0
#   C_yy = 1/(1 + 2*lambda*epsilon_dot) = 2/3
# beta = nu_s/(nu_s+nu_p) = 0.5 with nu_total = 0.1.
Simulation extensional_oldroyd_b D3Q19

Define epsilon_dot = 0.005

Domain L = 24 x 24 x 6  N = 24 x 24 x 6
Physics epsilon_dot = epsilon_dot
Rheology oldroyd_b { nu_s = 0.05 nu_p = 0.05 lambda = 50 }
Module viscoelastic

Run 1000 steps
